    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1627">

                <pb facs="1323" n="1207" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.73/3.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s instruction
                    No. 14, of the 15th instant, and to the Department’s telegram of December 16,
                    the Department <pb facs="1324" n="1208" xml:id="pg1208"/> encloses herewith for
                    your information and for appropriate action a copy of a letter dated December
                    13, 1911, from the Acting Secretary of the Navy in which is quoted the following
                    recommendation of the Joint Board of the Army and the Navy, dated November 27,
                    1911, and approved by the President under date of December 12, 1911: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>2. That an understanding be reached with Panama to prevent the
                            establishments of private and commercial wireless installations in its
                            territory.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>A copy of an unnumbered despatch,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1627-f1"/> dated November
                    29, 1911, from the American Consulate General at Panama on the same general
                    subject is also enclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>:) <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
